    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1499">

                <pb facs="1188" n="1178" xml:id="pg1178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363/6–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-23T17:00:00+08:00">June 23, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 23—9:20 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2442. Offices Standard-Vacuum Oil Company invaded today by large force former
                    temporary employees contractors associated with Standard-Vacuum. Workers demand
                    they be placed on Standard-Vacuum permanent payroll. Several foreign officials
                    barricaded in offices; other officials also threatened. Attitude workers
                    menacing. Labor Department SMCC and police so far have declined intervene. Labor
                    situation here appears to be gradually getting out-of-hand with officials
                    indifferent to situations bordering on anarchy where large industrial firms both
                    foreign and Chinese concerned.</p>
                <p>Repeated Nanking 1320, Canton 785.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
